    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d424">

                <pb facs="0530" n="458" xml:id="pg458"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 6369/317B.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Consul Moffat.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-12-02"><hi rendition="#italic">December 2,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Knox quotes for the information of Mr. Moffat the note delivered yesterday to
                    the then chargé d’affaires in Nicaragua.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d424-f1"/></p>
                <p>Directs him to make clear to the revolutionary leaders their obligation as
                    expressed above as well as our willingness to hold unofficially communication
                    with them.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
